<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,864,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,864,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 02/19/97    02/12/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,864,000  30,477,000    26,774,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 127,996     162,403	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   02/19/97    02/12/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,524,000   4,879,000     4,508,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,285,000   5,108,000     4,606,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,012,000   5,158,000     4,682,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,312,000   3,327,000     2,625,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,307,000   4,221,000     3,410,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,169,000   5,484,000     4,997,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,255,000   2,300,000     1,946,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,864,000  30,477,000    26,774,000</p>
